{"author":{"id":"f4e4dbe251fbd7519eab696986bae317e93a786739d6cebe9c4c1e89dd44e465"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1793513529,"nonce":"K1PLUjhWTFmof5jK6XB+A9p6fLo=","title":"M2: Port the Lean 4 kernel to C# (LeanSharp.Kernel)","message":"Parent epic: listed in a comment below. Depends on M1.\n\n\nA type-checking kernel ported function by function from Lean 4's C++ `src/kernel/` at tag v4.33.1 (commit `819816b`, the toolchain that produced init-medium), with Ansatz's Java kernel as a second reference. It is the trusted base for every later proof. `docs/kernel.md` maps each C++ file to its C# counterpart:\n\n| C++ | C# |\n|---|---|\n| `level.cpp` | `LevelOps.cs` |\n| `instantiate.cpp`, `abstract.cpp`, … | `ExprOps.cs` |\n| `type_checker.cpp` | `TypeChecker.cs`, `TypeChecker.Whnf.cs`, `TypeChecker.DefEq.cs` |\n| `inductive.cpp` | `Inductive.cs` |\n| `environment.cpp`, quotients | `Kernel.cs` |\n| Lean's `Replay` | `ExportChecker.cs` |\n\n`ExportChecker` does not trust exported recursors: it admits inductive blocks from types and constructors only and requires the generated constants to equal the exported ones up to binder names.\n\nDeliberate differences from Lean (kernel.md): fuel (20M interactive, 100M corpus; exhaustion is a resource limit, never acceptance), no `Lean.reduceBool`/`reduceNat` (so `native_decide` is rejected), a 512 MB-stack kernel thread, accumulated local context, macro scopes in generated names not modelled.\n\n\nAll 5,118 init-medium constants pass; arena negatives are rejected; then full Init.\n\n\n- Commits `2706651c6be1a5250f540fd0e6a4d15194ee5862` (kernel port) and `eb025ddd859e4022ecd238e0359573f8a7ed5e42` (full Init).\n- kernel.md results: full Init (Lean 4.33.1, 57,977 declarations / 59,433 constants) all accepted in ≈73 s; init-medium accepted ≈3 s; arena `002_badDef`, `141_falseFromUnsafe`, `proj-of-subst-prop` (lean4#14807) and `rec-of-subst-prop` (lean4#14847) rejected as Lean rejects them.\n- `SoundnessTests.cs` tampers with real declarations (wrong proofs, flipped K flag, swapped computation rules, missing recursor, forged quotient, …); each must be rejected for the expected reason and has a positive control.\n- Full Init is opt-in: `AcceptsFullInit` runs when `LEANSHARP_INIT_EXPORT` points to an export from `scripts/export-lean-library.sh`.\n\nStatus: complete (design §11 marks it ✅). Tests were not re-run when this ticket was filed (sandbox blocked `dotnet test`).\n\n\n- Mathlib (707,508 declarations at v4.33.1) has not been checked; it is the M3 stretch goal and is tracked on that ticket.\n- The Ansatz-compatible definitional-equality tracing described in design §7.1 is not implemented (no trace code in `src/`). Tracked on M3 as a follow-up.","files":null}]}